course: dictionary
lesson: 13710
title: One instance, one example
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An instance is one example of something, or one time it happens. When you want to prove a point, you give an instance. «Mia is a very kind friend.» To show she really is, add an instance: «For instance, she lent me her pencil case when mine broke.»
explain: «For instance» means «for example». Writers and teachers use it to share a clear case that supports what they say. When you see it in a text, the words after it give you the example.
explain: «In this instance» means «in this case»: one special situation, not every situation. «The rule is no phones in class, but in this instance the teacher let Sam check the time.» Only this one case was different.
explain: «In the first instance» means at first, as the first step, and it often appears in formal writing. «In the first instance, call the school office if you are going to be late.» Read the words around the phrase and the meaning will become clear.
fact: An instance is one example or one case of something happening.
fact: «For instance» means «for example».
fact: «In this instance» means «in this case».
fact: «In the first instance» means at first, as the first step.
fact: In maths, an instance of a pattern is one case that follows it: 2, 4 and 6 are instances of even numbers.
exercise: «Ben is good at sport. For instance, he won the school sprint on Friday.» What does «for instance» mean here? | Never again | *For example | For a long time | Far away from home
exercise: Mum says, «Our dog loves walks. For instance, he ran three miles with us on Sunday.» What is the instance? | Our dog loves walks | Sunday is a day of the week | *He ran three miles with us on Sunday | Mum
exercise: «In this instance, the teacher let us stay inside because it was raining.» What does «in this instance» mean? | Inside the school building | In the first place of many | Always, every time | *In this case
test: «Lily is always helpful. For instance, she carried the bags for the old lady.» What is one instance of Lily being helpful? | Lily is always helpful | She lives on a farm | *She carried the bags for the old lady | She is a teacher
test: «In the first instance, read the question twice.» What does «in the first instance» mean? | In a loud voice | *At first, as the first step | At the very end | Only if you are stuck
exam: Which phrase means «for example»? | In the first instance | In this instance | *For instance | At the same time
